.firecrawl/

# Graphify machine-local state (outputs themselves are committed)
**/graphify-out/cache/
**/graphify-out/.graphify_python
**/graphify-out/.graphify_root
**/graphify-out/20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# ZILF build output
verification/build/

# Third-party reference material — read locally, never vendored or redistributed.
# Holds the Comic Chat paper, the Z-Machine Standard, and ZILF/ZLR sources.
# ZILF is GPL-3.0 and ZLR ships no license at all; committing any of it would
# contradict NOTICE and this repository's Apache-2.0 licensing.
reference/

# Legacy path — the Comic Chat paper now lives in reference/ (kept so an old
# checkout with the file still in docs/ does not accidentally commit it).
docs/comic-chat-paper.md

# Comic Chat build outputs — untracked 2026-07-20 ahead of making this repo
# public. These are compiled artifacts of source that is already in the tree,
# plus one vendored Sun JDK 1.1.4 that Microsoft's MIT grant does not cover.
# Source, documentation, and comic art (.avb/.bmp/.gif/.jpg/.ico) stay tracked.
# Local copies are kept on disk; they are simply no longer version-controlled.
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.exe
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.dll
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.ocx
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.lib
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.class
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.map
original-projects/comic-chat/**/*.sym
original-projects/comic-chat/artifacts/jchat/jdk114/lib/classes.zip
/.playwright-cli
/graphify-out

# Playwright CLI session artifacts (snapshots, console logs) — driving the page
# is part of the workflow; its scratch output is not.
.playwright-cli/

# Vendored third-party Claude Code skills — local tooling, not part of what this
# repository ships. The project's own agent rules live in AGENTS.md.
.claude/skills/

# The world document, copied into the site by the Pages build (§6.5-beta) and by
# a local `wrangler pages dev` run. Generated from `ir/artifacts/`, never edited.
web/world/

# Wrangler local state — the local D1 replica used to test Pages Functions (6.8b).
# Never committed: it is a scratch database, and it is per-machine.
.wrangler/

# The built A/B page: it embeds every plate as a data URI and runs to megabytes.
# It regenerates with `npx tsx ab.ts`; the template and the PNGs are committed.
# (Generated SVG output is already covered by `art/vector/.gitignore`.)
art/vector/ab/index.html
